cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Kosh — offline, air-sealed secrets & API-key manager"
message: "If you use Kosh, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vamsi
    given-names: Deepak
repository-code: "https://github.com/deepakvamsi/kosh"
url: "https://deepakvamsi.github.io/kosh/"
abstract: >-
  Kosh is a free, open-source, air-sealed offline secrets manager for API keys,
  tokens, key pairs, logins, secure notes, and secret files. It keeps every
  credential in one encrypted local database (Argon2id + XChaCha20-Poly1305
  envelope encryption) with a tamper-evident, hash-chained audit log, and makes
  zero network connections by design. Cross-platform desktop app for Windows,
  macOS, and Linux, built in Go and Wails.
keywords:
  - secrets-manager
  - password-manager
  - api-key-manager
  - credential-manager
  - offline
  - air-gapped
  - local-first
  - encryption
  - argon2id
  - xchacha20-poly1305
  - go
  - wails
  - cross-platform
license: Apache-2.0
